"heptapod@gmail.com" <heptapod@gmail.com> wrote:
> I haven't played NetHack in quite some time. Decided to compile it with odd results.
>
> First, I played level one unpatched. Went to save and got this on my screen:
>
> http://i.imgur.com/xU6YTOm.png
>
> When I started my game again, everything was saved. What's going on here?

Your version has defined COMPRESS which means it wants to compress the
save file. "Exec to compress ... failed." means that it didn't find
the executable to compress the save file.

So a save file was generated and that's why you had no problem when
loading the game up again. For Windows, the easiest approach is to
comment out the COMPRESS define in include/config.h.

> Finally, I went to apply the statuscolors patch and got a bunch of lovely failed hunks.
>
> adrian@rastaban:/usr/games/lib/nethackdir$ sudo patch p1 < nh343-statuscolors.patch

You forgot a single character:
sudo patch -p1 < nh343-statuscolors.patch

-p1, not p1.

